+    # Bare-store self-heal: git needs HEAD + objects/ + refs/ to treat a directory as a
+    # repository.  A store that loses one of them reports `fatal: not a git repository`
+    # for EVERY command -- including the `git gc` of the next prune, so it never repairs
+    # itself and every checkpoint fails silently (#65349, #83036).  Upstream's only
+    # repair lives inside Pruner.reclaim(), behind a gc call that raises on failure, so a
+    # failed or timed-out gc skips it entirely.  The repair is a cheap mkdir-if-missing:
+    # run it proactively before every git invocation once the store exists.
+    if _store_has_head(store):
+        _repair_bare_repo_dirs(store)
+
